0009: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0010:     """Copy the marked sprite window into the marked empty window, aligned by the shared marker.
0011: 
0012:     Input structure
0013:     - The dominant color is the outer background.
0014:     - There are exactly two solid rectangular non-background windows.
0015:     - Each window has one pixel of a shared marker color; only one window also
0016:       contains the sprite color(s).
0017: 
0018:     Rule
0019:     - The marker-only window gives the output size and fill color.
0020:     - Translate every non-fill pixel from the sprite window so the source marker
0021:       lands on the destination marker.
0022: 
0023:     Key insight
0024:     The two equal marker pixels define the offset; the output is cropped to the
0025:     marker-only window, not to the sprite window.
